1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,453
Good evening from the OROS closing desk.

2
00:00:03,453 --> 00:00:08,719
Time to grade this morning's call — the part most shows skip.

3
00:00:08,719 --> 00:00:10,360
Daily Journal Corp.

4
00:00:10,360 --> 00:00:16,748
(S.C.), ticker DJCO triggered, then faded to -2.9 percent below the entry.

5
00:00:16,748 --> 00:00:21,755
If it closes a week below the stop, the exit is automatic.

6
00:00:21,755 --> 00:00:25,208
That is not a failure; that is the plan.

7
00:00:25,208 --> 00:00:30,144
Why we grade in public: a forecast that is never checked is just content.

8
00:00:30,144 --> 00:00:35,553
Every morning call gets an evening verdict, and both go in the permanent record.

9
00:00:35,518 --> 00:00:39,763
On the day, the book is up 193 dollars.

10
00:00:39,763 --> 00:00:46,294
Charles Schwab Corporation (The) (SCHW) leads, +2.3 percent.

11
00:00:46,294 --> 00:00:51,191
Atlanta Braves Holdings (BATRK) lags at -2.0.

12
00:00:51,191 --> 00:00:57,069
The checklist is clear: nothing requires action today.

13
00:00:57,069 --> 00:01:00,596
On screen, the day's gainers and laggards inside the paper book.

14
00:01:00,552 --> 00:01:08,815
And here is the book itself — the actual holdings, identical to this morning's emailed report.

15
00:01:08,815 --> 00:01:18,925
12 positions, led by AbbVie, ticker ABBV, Eli Lilly and, ticker LLY, State Street SPDR S&P Biotech ETF, ticker XBI.

16
00:01:18,925 --> 00:01:30,880
Every line carries its share count, its entry, and its exit — because a position without a defined exit is not a position, it is a hope.

17
00:01:30,831 --> 00:01:35,514
Now the part that makes this system different: the loop.

18
00:01:35,514 --> 00:01:37,856
Every morning OROS proposes.

19
00:01:37,856 --> 00:01:48,142
Every evening it grades its own call, journals the verdict, and adjusts its own risk before it is allowed to propose again.

20
00:01:48,142 --> 00:01:51,989
Inside the book today: 9 positions up, 3 down.

21
00:01:51,989 --> 00:01:54,330
Best, SCHW at +2.29 percent.

22
00:01:54,330 --> 00:01:56,170
Worst, BATRK at -1.98.

23
00:01:56,170 --> 00:02:01,021
Both go in the journal — wins and losses get the same ink.

24
00:02:01,021 --> 00:02:07,962
The honest scoreboard reads: expectancy -8.11% per trade over 207 graded positions.

25
00:02:07,962 --> 00:02:14,819
Because that record is soft, the system has throttled itself to 25% position size.

26
00:02:14,819 --> 00:02:19,837
Nobody told it to — full size must be earned back with wins.

27
00:02:19,837 --> 00:02:31,879
What tonight's read hands to tomorrow's open: 240 names close the day in Stage 2; position size stays cut to 25% until the record earns it back.

28
00:02:31,853 --> 00:02:34,112
Over to the sports desk.

29
00:02:34,112 --> 00:02:43,432
Day 35 of the race: three books, the same one hundred thousand simulated dollars, since July sixth.

30
00:02:43,432 --> 00:02:49,740
In first place, the live self-rebuilding book, in blue, at 102,175.

31
00:02:49,740 --> 00:02:55,294
Then the index fund, in gray, 0.3 thousand back at 101,922.

32
00:02:55,294 --> 00:03:02,543
Then the frozen first portfolio, the green line, 2.5 thousand back at 99,675.

33
00:03:02,543 --> 00:03:05,179
The race has no finish line.

34
00:03:05,179 --> 00:03:09,509
Same books, same dollars, back at it tomorrow.

35
00:03:09,509 --> 00:03:14,404
Every line starts the same day with the same dollar.

36
00:03:14,404 --> 00:03:16,287
Nothing is restated.

37
00:03:16,287 --> 00:03:18,617
Today's lesson is benchmarking.

38
00:03:18,617 --> 00:03:25,078
Any strategy must beat the boring alternative: the same money parked in an index fund.

39
00:03:25,078 --> 00:03:28,535
That is why the S and P line shares the chart.

40
00:03:28,535 --> 00:03:37,551
If the system cannot outrun it, the index deserves the money, and publishing the race every day keeps the system honest.

41
00:03:37,510 --> 00:03:44,845
All figures are simulated paper trading, graded and journaled by the OROS agents with no human intervention.

42
00:03:44,845 --> 00:03:47,086
Nothing here is financial advice.

43
00:03:47,086 --> 00:03:50,075
From the closing desk — see you at the open.
